{"at": "2026-09-09T09:39:20.890834+00:00", "event_id": "01M22RJH5T92YW48GK8ES5XFA9", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M22R47KGCH8DQYB4GM2TMTXQ", "final_answer": "Both paths (y/p in-app and Ctrl+C/Ctrl+V system clipboard), selected by a configuration option toggling between 'normal' (Ctrl+C/V) and 'vim' key bindings. Configuration persisted in the OS-typical user config location. The setting also governs the content editor: with vim bindings it gets a vim-style insert mode entered with 'i' etc. A new File top-bar menu entry opens a config editor (initially only the key-binding choice).", "mission_id": "01M22R1ESWGJN19C8X7SKS1N1G", "mission_slug": "asn1-tree-delete-copy-paste-01M22R1E", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": true, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-09-09T09:39:20.890834Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M22R47KGCH8DQYB4GM2TMTXQ", "state_entered_at": "2026-09-09T09:39:20.889719Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
{"at": "2026-09-09T09:39:41.187808+00:00", "event_id": "01M22RK503N4XK736WE6H6PFFB", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M22RK502WGQNATNRXR2WWWC8", "input_key": "vim_editor_depth", "mission_id": "01M22R1ESWGJN19C8X7SKS1N1G", "mission_slug": "asn1-tree-delete-copy-paste-01M22R1E", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["Modal core: normal/insert modes, hjkl/0/$ motion, x, v visual selection, y/d/p, u undo", "Insert-mode toggle only: i enters typing, Esc leaves it, everything else unchanged", "Other"], "origin_flow": "specify", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "SPECIFY", "question": "With vim key bindings configured, how much of vim's modal editing do the value editors (hex, text, integer, OID ...) adopt?", "recorded_at": "2026-09-09T09:39:41.187808Z", "run_id": "01M22RK502WGQNATNRXR2WWWC8", "state_entered_at": "2026-09-09T09:39:41.186739Z", "step_id": "specify.vim-bindings.editor-depth"}}
{"at": "2026-09-09T09:45:08.350774+00:00", "event_id": "01M22RX4FY0JNNHE4XZCX193HR", "event_type": "DecisionPointResolved", "payload": {"actual_participants": [], "closed_locally_while_widened": false, "closure_message": null, "decision_point_id": "01M22RK502WGQNATNRXR2WWWC8", "final_answer": "Modal core (normal/insert modes, i/a/I/A, Esc, h/j/k/l/0/$, x, v visual, y/d/p, u). In vim bindings Ctrl+C/X/V/Z do NOT act as in normal bindings; Ctrl+A increments and Ctrl+X decrements the number under the cursor as in vim. The vim key-binding space must stay free of normal-mode artifacts so more vim functions can be added later.", "mission_id": "01M22R1ESWGJN19C8X7SKS1N1G", "mission_slug": "asn1-tree-delete-copy-paste-01M22R1E", "mission_type": "software-dev", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "other_answer": true, "rationale": null, "recorded_at": "2026-09-09T09:45:08.350774Z", "resolved_by": "cli", "run_id": "01M22RK502WGQNATNRXR2WWWC8", "state_entered_at": "2026-09-09T09:45:08.349596Z", "summary": null, "terminal_outcome": "resolved"}}
